{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793741793,"nonce":"BI0SIKDZqh+NVbeMpXekytbTL9w=","message":"Also evaluate bytecode register-slot reuse from liveness: compile_function currently assigns one register to every HIR SSA value, including values on untaken branches. Even after symbol caching, the 24-site fixture costs 211 ns/call versus 103 ns for the small fixture, so unused-register setup remains visible. This is evidence to investigate, not an isolated measurement of slot allocation. Reusing slots must preserve parallel phi copies, per-call GC read sets, undef checks and OSR live-in mappings, and its lowering cost must be included in cold-start measurements. It may also help the \u003e65535-values limit tracked by dfe7689.","files":null}]}